    {
      "id": "H-004",
      "title": "Admin Token API Endpoint Enables Account Lockout DoS and Lacks CAPTCHA/IP Rate Limiting",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "attack_complexity": {
        "rating": "low",
        "authentication": "none",
        "user_interaction": "none",
        "prerequisites": [],
        "rationale": "Account lockout DoS requires only 6 unauthenticated POST requests. Slow brute-force is feasible at 6 attempts/30min. No CAPTCHA or IP blocking exists on API."
      },
      "category": "authentication",
      "cwe": "CWE-307",
      "description": "POST /V1/integration/admin/token is anonymous and protected only by per-username lockout (6 failures \u2192 30min lock). No IP-based rate limiting or CAPTCHA exists on the API. An attacker can intentionally lock any admin account by sending 6 invalid requests, causing denial of service. The lockout is per-username in oauth_token_request_log table, independent of admin UI lockout in admin_user table.",
      "location": {
        "file": "app/code/Magento/Integration/etc/webapi.xml",
        "lines": "N/A",
        "function": "createAdminAccessToken"
      },
      "attack_vector": "POST /rest/V1/integration/admin/token with username/password.",
      "impact": {
        "primary": "Denial of service: any admin account can be locked for 30 minutes by sending 6 unauthenticated requests. Repeated attacks keep the account permanently locked.",
        "additional": [
          "Slow brute-force: 6 passwords tested per 30-minute window, indefinitely, from any IP",
          "Timing-based username enumeration via Argon2 hash check timing difference"
        ],
        "severity_justification": "Downgraded from HIGH to MEDIUM because per-username lockout with 30min timeout does prevent rapid brute-force. However, the account lockout DoS and lack of IP rate limiting are significant for production. Admin passwords are typically long enough to resist 6-per-30min brute-force."
      },
      "remediation": "Add IP-based rate limiting (e.g., nginx rate limit or WAF rule). Add CAPTCHA after N failures. Consider exponential backoff instead of fixed lockout. Implement constant-time username lookup to prevent timing enumeration.",
      "evidence": {
        "source_validated": true
      },
      "validation_status": "confirmed",
      "discovered_by": "task_002",
      "discovered_at": "2026-03-27T12:25:00-04:00",
      "technical_details": "RequestThrottler (Integration/Model/Oauth/Token/RequestThrottler.php) tracks failures per-username in oauth_token_request_log table. Default config: max_failures_count=6, timeout=1800s (30min).\n\nFlow: createAdminAccessToken() \u2192 throttle() checks failures count \u2192 login() authenticates \u2192 on failure: incrementFailuresCount() \u2192 on success: resetFailuresCount().\n\nKey weaknesses:\n1. No IP-based rate limiting \u2014 attacker can lock any admin account with 6 requests from any IP\n2. No CAPTCHA on API endpoint (only admin UI login has CAPTCHA)  \n3. API lockout (oauth_token_request_log) and admin UI lockout (admin_user table) are INDEPENDENT \u2014 locking API doesn't lock UI and vice versa\n4. Timing side-channel: valid usernames trigger loadByUsername() + Argon2 verifyIdentity(); invalid usernames skip the hash check, creating measurable timing difference (~100ms+ for Argon2)\n5. After lock expires, failures_count resets to 0 (clearExpiredFailures cron), allowing indefinite slow brute-force at 6 attempts per 30-minute window\n\nCredential validation: CredentialsValidator only checks non-empty username/password. No complexity or format validation on API input.",
      "affected_files": [
        "app/code/Magento/Integration/Model/AdminTokenService.php",
        "app/code/Magento/Integration/Model/Oauth/Token/RequestThrottler.php",
        "app/code/Magento/Integration/Model/ResourceModel/Oauth/Token/RequestLog.php",
        "app/code/Magento/Integration/etc/webapi.xml",
        "app/code/Magento/Integration/etc/config.xml"
      ],
      "affected_functions": [
        "createAdminAccessToken",
        "throttle",
        "incrementFailuresCount",
        "getFailuresCount"
      ],
      "environment_relevance": "production",
      "poc": {
        "type": "curl",
        "steps": "for i in $(seq 1 6); do curl -s -X POST https://target/rest/V1/integration/admin/token -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"wrong$i\"}'; done",
        "expected_result": "After 6 requests, the admin account is locked for 30 minutes. Subsequent valid login attempts via API return the same error.",
        "destructive": false,
        "auth_required": "none"
      },
      "validation_notes": "Validated by reading RequestThrottler, RequestLog, AdminTokenService source. Per-username lockout confirmed with 6 failures/30min defaults. No IP-based protection. Account lockout DoS confirmed trivially exploitable.",
      "validated_at": "2026-03-27T20:15:00-04:00",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "is_gadget": true,
      "gadget_type": "account_lockout_dos",
      "chains_with": [
